# DTF tier manifest: nexus-group-virtual  (issue #2783)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=nexus (same real-Nexus topology
# as the `migration` tier: a live Sonatype Nexus 3 migration source next to the
# backend on the slot's own DTF network; health-gated ~2-3 min boot).
#
# WHAT THIS DISCRIMINATES (#2783): Nexus `group` repositories did NOT correlate
# to AK `virtual` repos on migration — the group migrated to a virtual repo with
# ZERO members (the member links were never written). The #2783 fix captures the
# Nexus group's memberNames, correlates each source member name to the id of its
# already-migrated AK repo, and writes virtual_repo_members in order (skipping
# absent members, no dangling rows). The oracle seeds 2+ hosted repos AND a
# `group` repo whose members are those hosted repos, runs a REAL AK migration,
# and asserts (DB): the group migrates to an AK repo with repo_type='virtual'
# whose virtual_repo_members are exactly the migrated AK repo ids of the member
# repos, in order — and that there are no dangling member rows.
# NON-ZERO-WHILE-BUG: pre-#2783 the virtual has 0 members -> oracle asserts the
# member rows exist + match, so it exits 0 only on the fixed image.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives admin login + repeated migration
# REST calls back-to-back through one admin user; matches the migration tier's
# rig posture (§2.2: relax a shipped control explicitly; base default stays ON).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.nexus"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
